WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.707
Use this guide when deciding how to reshape.

00:00:02.707 --> 00:00:08.052
If category values should become columns, pivot with conditional aggregation.

00:00:08.052 --> 00:00:13.172
If columns should become rows, use UNION ALL or lateral VALUES.

00:00:13.172 --> 00:00:16.447
Keep dynamic categories long when possible.

00:00:16.447 --> 00:00:19.757
Use a wide form for stable matrix reporting.

00:00:19.757 --> 00:00:25.817
And whenever several source rows map to one cell, make the aggregate decision explicit.

00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:31.982
Connect this idea to a BI dashboard turning monthly categories into presentation columns.

00:00:31.982 --> 00:00:37.632
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:37.632 --> 00:00:45.412
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:51.032
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:51.032 --> 00:00:56.800
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
